// What a placed Silhouette does when its Silhouette has a graph. A Silhouette's graph (graph.json beside its
// root.calamus, edited in the editor's Event Graph tab) is built into a class in game-graphs/generated/ that derives
// from this one, such as `ScriptedLampBehaviour`. Each event node in the graph becomes the override of one of these
// methods, so a method the graph has no event for does nothing.
//
// The level makes one for every placed entity whose `silhouette` property names a Silhouette with a graph
// (GraphBehaviours:::Create), so each placed copy has its own fields: a graph variable keeps its value from one frame to
// the next for that copy alone, as a Blueprint variable does.
SilhouetteBehaviour :: class {
public:
    // The placed root this behaviour belongs to, the `entity` pin of every event.
    entity: i64;

    SilhouetteBehaviour~: (entity: i64) : entity(entity) { }

    // Once, when the level has loaded.
    virtual BeginPlay~: () -> void { }

    // Once per display frame while the game is playing. `frameTime` is the real time the frame took, in seconds.
    virtual Update~: (frameTime: f32) -> void { }

    // Once per fixed simulation step, with `fixedStepTime` always 1/60 s.
    virtual FixedUpdate~: (fixedStepTime: f32) -> void { }
}
